# Line endings are pinned to LF for every text file, with no per-platform
# exceptions.
#
# Two concrete reasons, not style preference:
#
#  1. The WordPress Coding Standards ruleset wired up in phpcs.xml includes
#     Generic.Files.LineEndings, which requires "\n". CRLF working copies would
#     fail phpcs on every file, and driving phpcs to zero is a Phase 7 gate.
#  2. This machine has core.autocrlf=true. Without this file the next checkout
#     rewrites all tracked sources as CRLF, and a later `git add --renormalize`
#     would produce a spurious whole-repo diff.
#
# Keeping .ps1 on LF too is deliberate: PowerShell reads LF fine, and one rule
# with no exceptions is easier to reason about than a platform matrix.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Generated by bin/build-address-data.php — still text, still LF.
data/**/*.php text eol=lf

# Binaries must never be touched.
*.png  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif  binary
*.ico  binary
*.svg  text eol=lf
*.woff  binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ttf   binary
*.zip   binary
*.mo    binary
